    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Heptăpylos</span></b> , on
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>c.</i>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> , n.), adj., =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑπτάπυλος</span>, <i>seven-gated</i>, an epithet of the city of Thebes: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thebas Heptapylos accessimus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 146</span></i>
			.—Also in Latinized form: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cadmus Thebas Heptapylas condidit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg.
					F. 275</span></i>
			.</div>
